---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../config/site';
import { getWriting } from '../lib/content';

// The sentence about issue one appears only once there is a piece to point at.
const [latest] = await getWriting();
---

<Base
  title="About"
  description="David Hynes reads the terms behind the AI and software in hospitality venues and writes down what they say about a group's data."
  current="about"
>
  <header class="plain-head">
    <div class="wrap"><h1>About</h1></div>
  </header>
  <div class="wrap plain-body">
    <div class="md indent">
      <p>
        I am David Hynes, in Melbourne. I read the terms and price lists behind the AI and software that run hospitality
        venues, and I write down what they say about a group’s data, its fees and what it costs to leave. I quote the
        clause and date the page, because vendors change both.
      </p>
      {
        latest && (
          <p>
            Issue one covers Square: what its terms say about who keeps your sales records, and what you can export.
          </p>
        )
      }

      <h2>How I work</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <p>Every quote is word for word, with the document, the section and the date, so you can check it in two minutes.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>I keep three things apart: what a document says, what I infer (marked “my read”), and what I cannot tell you.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>A vendor’s marketing language is evidence. I quote it and date it. I do not use it as my own.</p>
        </li>
        <li>
          <p>
            Each piece ends with something you can paste into an email to the vendor: a question, a clause to check or a
            number to ask for.
          </p>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p>
        I have no sponsors and no affiliate links. If I misread a clause, tell me and I will correct it and <a href="/updates/">date the correction</a>.
      </p>

      <h2>Where I stand</h2>
      <p>
        You should know my interest. I am looking for a Head of AI role at a larger hospitality or food and beverage
        group, and I lean towards groups keeping their data in their own hands. Weigh what I write with that in mind.
      </p>

      <h2>Get in touch</h2>
      <p>
        If you run AI or operations at a group and want to talk, email me: <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a>. My other work is at <a href={site.portfolioUrl} rel="noopener">{site.portfolioUrl.replace('https://', '')}</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Base>
